{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyoTRBvzKgVSscNoe1GY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The flag adds a compatibility shim to the bundle. It's described in `scripts/build.py:6-7`: it writes `pkg/_legacy.py`, which makes the two current functions available under their old pre-1.0 names:\n\n- `group_totals` as `sum_by`\n- `parse_amount` as `to_decimal`\n\nSo code written against the pre-1.0 API, like `from pkg._legacy import sum_by`, keeps working.\n\n**What I couldn't find is why the runbook says to use it.** Step 2 gives its reason, but step 4 doesn't. Nothing else in the repo uses the old names: the only places \"legacy\" appears are the runbook line and `build.py` itself. The git history doesn't help either, because the flag was already there in the oldest commit I can see (`548363d Release 1.3.2`). So whether anyone still depends on the shim isn't recorded here. It would be outside users of the package, which this repo can't show.\n\nIt may well be cruft, but I can't confirm that from the repo, and dropping it is a breaking change for anyone still on the old names. Before removing it I'd check whether any downstream users import `pkg._legacy`. If none do, drop it in a release whose changelog says so, ideally a major version or at least with a deprecation notice first. 1.4.0 shipped with the shim, as the runbook says.\n\nIf you want it gone, I can remove the flag from step 4, along with the shim code in `build.py` if you like, and add a changelog entry. Just let me know."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":956,"cache_read_input_tokens":23802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":956},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool